{
  "body": "This is a call to discuss a frameworks to help aid with coordination between the various EVM-like L2s. The idea is to establish **optional** norms and standards for L2s to be able to extend the EVM and related tooling while limiting conflicts with the L1 EVM and preventing a proliferation of mutually incompatible standards among the L2s.\r\n\r\n## Meeting Info\r\n\r\n- [Wed Oct 18, 2023, 14:00-15:30 UTC](https://savvytime.com/converter/utc-to-germany-berlin-united-kingdom-london-ny-new-york-city-ca-san-francisco-china-shanghai-japan-tokyo-australia-sydney/oct-18-2023/2pm)\r\n- Zoom link shared on `RIP coordination` telegram channel shortly before the call (DM @CarlBeek on Telegram to be added)\r\n- Recording available on YouTube https://youtu.be/aPvMoVI6rFE\r\n\r\n\r\n## Agenda\r\n\r\n- General\r\n    - The RollCall vision\r\n    - RFC on schedule and timing\r\n    - Further discussion at L2 day in Istanbul\r\n- RIP standard\r\n    - General & process\r\n    - `secp256r1` precompile\r\n\r\n## Further discussion\r\n\r\nFeel free to add comments to this issue with further items of discussion",
